 "text": "Hello, how are things going? That's the bearings making friction with the rack. It' usually nothing to worry about, unless it gets louder or feels different. Be careful it doesn't get in the gears. A wet cloth and a little oil on the side is fine. Squirt a little on the side, then wipe with a clean rag so there's no drips. Don't get it on the gears. Clean it first with a dry rag, then go on from there. Not really, a little goes a long way. Just enough so the bearings don't squeal.",
